						<p class="pDate">Friday, July 05, 2002</p>
						<p class="pTitle">Do not get riped off by Koru 
						</p>
						<p class=pText>
						I recently wanted to come back to EQ so I started looking for a character to purchase.  I finally found one, a level 60 warrior named Koru.  I sent an XBox and eight games to the guy for the acount.  After I got the account I played it for a few days, all this time people are accusing me of hacking the account.  I eventually found out the account was stolen and then sold to me.  I was also locked out of the account and could not get back in.  Luckily I got the sellers number from someone in the game and called him... his dad picked up the phone.  His fater was unaware his son was selling stolen accounts and he did not know his son had an XBox.  Well, the guy mailed me my XBox back, but now I had half the number of games I sent, he traded some he said.  I also lost out on the shipping cost I paid to send the heavy XBox, and I had made a few characters on the account I purchased, which I lost also.  Mind you, these characters were loaded with good items like FBSS, Centi Longsword, and other items.  I messaged Koru in the game and he told me that his little brother deleted the characters with their items... yet within five minutes I saw one of the characters I made online.  So, thus the seller and the other guy who said he was the origional owner are both liars.  Do not buy a level 60 dwarf named Koru, he is not in full Warlord armor as advertised, he is nowhere near getting his epic, he does not have a good 2 hand slasher as advertised either.  Heck, at level 60 he has one of the worst haste items in the game.<BR>  The sellers name was Alan McGrath, so please be careful when you purchase or trade for any account.  I only posted here because I saw he was trying to ripoff someone else.  Good luck to all.
						<br>
						 - Zakk<BR><BR>
						</p>
